1
00:05:25,384 --> 00:05:31,384
Have you ever dreamt of a better version of yourself?

2
00:10:50,769 --> 00:10:56,769
The Substance is a horror, science fiction, thriller
film directed by Coralie Fargeat.

3
00:16:16,153 --> 00:16:22,153
A fading celebrity decides to use a black market drug, a cell-replicating
substance that temporarily creates a younger, better version of herself.

4
00:21:41,538 --> 00:21:47,538
Elisabeth, played by Demi Moore.

5
00:27:06,923 --> 00:27:12,923
Sue, played by Margaret Qualley.

6
00:32:32,307 --> 00:32:38,307
Harvey, played by Dennis Quaid.

7
00:37:57,692 --> 00:38:03,692
Fred, played by Edward Hamilton-Clark.

8
00:43:23,076 --> 00:43:29,076
Oliver, played by Gore Abrams.

9
00:48:48,461 --> 00:48:54,461
Troy, played by Oscar Lesage.

10
00:54:13,846 --> 00:54:19,846
The Substance is a 2024 body horror film written, directed,
co-produced, and co-edited by Coralie Fargeat.

11
00:59:39,230 --> 00:59:45,230
It stars Demi Moore, Margaret Qualley, and Dennis Quaid.

12
01:05:04,615 --> 01:05:10,615
The film follows a fading celebrity who is fired by her producer due to her age, and uses a black
market drug that creates a younger version of herself with unexpected side effects.

13
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
Fargeat wrote the screenplay to explore societal
pressures on women's bodies and aging.

14
01:15:55,384 --> 01:16:01,384
A co-production between France, the United Kingdom, and the United States,
principal photography took place in France from August to October 2022.

15
01:21:20,769 --> 01:21:26,769
Noted for its satirical elements and grotesque, hyperrealistic imagery, the film extensively utilised prosthetic makeup and
other practical effects such as suits, puppets, dummies, inserts, and approximately 21,000 liters (5,500 U.S.

16
01:26:46,153 --> 01:26:52,153
gallons) of fake blood.

17
01:32:11,538 --> 01:32:17,538
It was originally set to be distributed by Universal Pictures, but the rights were later acquired by Mubi after
Universal cancelled the distribution deal following a dispute with Fargeat over final cut privileges.

18
01:37:36,923 --> 01:37:42,923
The Substance premiered at the 77th Cannes Film Festival on May 19, 2024, where
it won Best Screenplay and was nominated for the Palme d'Or.

19
01:43:02,307 --> 01:43:08,307
The film was theatrically released in the United Kingdom and the United
States on September 20, 2024, and in France on November 6, 2024.

20
01:48:27,692 --> 01:48:33,692
It received widespread acclaim, with particular praise for Fargeat's writing
and directing, the special effects, and Moore's performance.

21
01:53:53,076 --> 01:53:59,076
At the box office, the film grossed $77–82 million on a budget of
$18 million, becoming Mubi's highest-grossing film.

22
01:59:18,461 --> 01:59:24,461
Among numerous other accolades, it won the Academy Award for Best Makeup and Hairstyling and Moore's performance earned her a Golden Globe
Award, Critics' Choice Award, and Screen Actors Guild Award, as well as nominations for an Academy Award and BAFTA Award.

23
02:04:43,846 --> 02:04:49,846
The film also received nominations for Best Picture and Best Director at
the Academy Awards, Critics’ Choice and Golden Globes.

24
02:10:09,230 --> 02:10:15,230
The film explores themes of new year's eve,
capitalism, birthday, black market, identity.

25
02:15:34,615 --> 02:15:40,615
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
